[{:db/id "q-342697/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "2caa8211-aa10-5c2c-ac0f-b503fca330b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342697/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5200f13-2722-519d-9cb5-2c9037f741b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342697/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-342697/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342697" :question/id #uuid "04ce6cd4-ddeb-529d-8ad4-fa72c75dbef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-342697" :question/problem "Given that $y={x}^{2}+1$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{2}$ at the point where $x=1,$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=1,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2(1) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342697/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "660e7de2-aeea-55ad-971b-3c137ccb1521"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342697"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48763/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "bf8efaad-ff7f-557a-82ec-b59320329551" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48763/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "219640de-61f8-5c51-9d90-ae8347329ca4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48763/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "3c032e1a-8171-5c9a-a00c-037b02a4d789" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48763/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "8d2fd07d-09a0-5b06-abdd-1ac91212267b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48763/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e28903c7-2b4d-5d8b-b073-a1759a196cdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48763/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "386fd468-c359-5029-adf3-c864b1246a39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48763/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-48763/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-48763/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-48763/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-48763/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-48763/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48763" :question/id #uuid "99ded3a6-6a92-5942-b8b9-2758a74bf429" :question/math-academy-id "q-48763" :question/problem "Given that $y=3x-1$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2$ at the point where $x=-1,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x-1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3x-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2$ and $x=-1,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2\\cdot (3)=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48763/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "660e7de2-aeea-55ad-971b-3c137ccb1521"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48763"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-313855/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "a6f8f08b-1209-5799-9f8e-3bea955840e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-313855/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a343f2e-3bce-59c0-8da8-32eb86e84161" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-313855/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-313855/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-313855" :question/id #uuid "65954d52-ea96-5390-9cfa-b0aa0d4101ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-313855" :question/problem "Given that $y=-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-3$ at the point where $x=2,$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-3{x}^{2}+8x-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-3$ and $x=2,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (-3\\cdot (2)^{2}+8\\cdot (2)-5)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-313855/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "660e7de2-aeea-55ad-971b-3c137ccb1521"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-313855"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-48765"] :question/problem "Given that $y=2{x}^{3}-2x$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1$ at the point where $x=-2,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{3}-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (6{x}^{2}-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1$ and $x=-2,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =1\\cdot (6\\cdot (-2)^{2}-2)=22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-48770/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "c55a9e1f-26d9-5d8e-8739-f4dd43517b1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48770/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "67235440-2ef6-502e-925f-fc1765bd7190" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48770/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "d066b761-6e5a-5c4d-824b-2ce26ae4c025" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48770/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "bcbedfc5-c2f4-5a20-8604-24e29a3db98d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48770/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "36c304d3-7506-5de2-9e0c-9375f344b29e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48770/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7b0147d-7e62-50a3-9fe6-3ae59372a583" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48770/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer-field/choices ["q-48770/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-48770/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-48770/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-48770/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-48770/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48770" :question/id #uuid "370da794-2fe1-5503-abab-e6edee8fbed0" :question/math-academy-id "q-48770" :question/problem "Given that $y=3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3$ at the point where $x=-1,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (12{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3$ and $x=-1,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (12(-1)^{3}+6(-1)^{2}) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-6) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48770/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "660e7de2-aeea-55ad-971b-3c137ccb1521"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48770"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342707/field-1/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" :answer/id #uuid "f34f2e68-cc30-5ff0-ba8e-4fdbcfcba323" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342707/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e23473b-40c0-5f4a-acb0-ed41789a883d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342707/field-1/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-342707/field-1/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342707" :question/id #uuid "64ac928e-3cbc-5fc3-997c-9cc3278a4024" :question/math-academy-id "q-342707" :question/problem "Given that $r=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{3}$ at the point where $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\,(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot [-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})] \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342707/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f2818fc-787e-5b46-8a7a-c5fbea7905a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342707"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-48806"] :question/problem "Given that $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\sqrt{2}$ at the point where $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-313637/field-1/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "41ec6b23-5b91-5145-83e4-a2817d50c2c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-313637/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b94ebd69-7893-5c7e-8d1e-56ec03b81f89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-313637/field-1/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer-field/choices ["q-313637/field-1/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-313637" :question/id #uuid "ab4ba7d5-a8ac-5c4e-b369-4be7306d4fc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-313637" :question/problem "Given that $r=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta $ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=-3$ at the point where $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=-3$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (5\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot 5\\cdot (\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-313637/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f2818fc-787e-5b46-8a7a-c5fbea7905a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-313637"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48801/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "7011cdc9-c928-50da-a7d3-37837e18594c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48801/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "e395562f-c6d2-5457-81a9-0d4a92b793c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48801/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "467ac5c5-9524-5a04-b66d-a0d45eac05db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48801/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "5d931791-f111-5ed7-a6fd-cd99c0140829" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48801/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "f2419fee-a1bb-5863-8bcb-37159e5f55e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48801/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a86d8903-3244-5b9d-8be3-2d32d72dc3be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48801/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-48801/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-48801/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-48801/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-48801/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" "q-48801/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48801" :question/id #uuid "55e8556a-5ae1-5690-852b-2dad76c68111" :question/math-academy-id "q-48801" :question/problem "Given that $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2$ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=-3$ at the point where $\\theta =\\pi ,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=-3$ and $\\theta =\\pi ,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48801/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f2818fc-787e-5b46-8a7a-c5fbea7905a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48801"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115772/selection/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer/id #uuid "5