t to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}-6x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}-6x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-6x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (2x-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=3\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =3\\cdot (2\\cdot 2-6)\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s} \\\\  & =-6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72231/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b47a8b7-722d-564e-8e7a-ad07577d6f6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72231"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342740/field-1/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" :answer/id #uuid "88249f5d-1501-5c65-bc86-b1554d487123" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342740/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d65adfe-9a18-55f9-8b16-3b13e206af06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342740/field-1/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" :answer-field/choices ["q-342740/field-1/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342740" :question/id #uuid "37812340-9e80-5efe-8a6b-2a539b36a5af" :question/math-academy-id "q-342740" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2}$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=3\\,\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nThe $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2}] \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2}] \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x+1}+2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-4\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3+1}+2(3)) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}+6) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{25}{4} \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of $-25\\text{ }\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342740/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b47a8b7-722d-564e-8e7a-ad07577d6f6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342740"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115785/selection/9b0bfe953619d9f151476ad115967037572cb28a56f4cfae70162f2c5907a4d8" :answer/id #uuid "dbe5cc47-b230-5df6-95c8-6891c755c1dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-36\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115785/selection/e22269ae6fb7da94b4ab00cc6a509fadf3871059c5683bd4f43fa07492f75421" :answer/id #uuid "053998b1-258e-5c72-b962-ff5bd0686a3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-30\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115785/selection/a1eba922e744758ee2e404d7043b98efc157ab3ab8dab2d72fb99cee191c951d" :answer/id #uuid "1992e8f0-106c-5bd5-9914-b069c6483c59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-31\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115785/selection/630c21b300f71701c63549f779a0e6ba1f33baabf63b28abbac418b4d77bafe2" :answer/id #uuid "c2119d83-541a-5f16-ae1e-2f38538ce58a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-33\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115785/selection/9c085f4df5b1039407c01b37810ff96785826800534dce62d2bac15bf30dd9c0" :answer/id #uuid "e3ec4cef-b55d-5d61-bb3d-5b7f82271c1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115785/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd883779-7539-5c1f-9efe-6d9aecbb2766" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115785/selection/a1eba922e744758ee2e404d7043b98efc157ab3ab8dab2d72fb99cee191c951d" :answer-field/choices ["q-115785/selection/9b0bfe953619d9f151476ad115967037572cb28a56f4cfae70162f2c5907a4d8" "q-115785/selection/e22269ae6fb7da94b4ab00cc6a509fadf3871059c5683bd4f43fa07492f75421" "q-115785/selection/a1eba922e744758ee2e404d7043b98efc157ab3ab8dab2d72fb99cee191c951d" "q-115785/selection/630c21b300f71701c63549f779a0e6ba1f33baabf63b28abbac418b4d77bafe2" "q-115785/selection/9c085f4df5b1039407c01b37810ff96785826800534dce62d2bac15bf30dd9c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115785" :question/id #uuid "50fb4f97-5980-53b3-b2fc-bf511f707ff7" :question/math-academy-id "q-115785" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=4{x}^{3}+16x$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=3\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4{x}^{3}+16x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{x}^{3}+16x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{3}+16x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (12{x}^{2}+16).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =(-\\frac{1}{4})\\cdot (12\\cdot (3)^{2}+16)\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s} \\\\  & =-31\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115785/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b47a8b7-722d-564e-8e7a-ad07577d6f6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115785"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72227/selection/3d84380a08212e1f89ee8af17779262184458ad276b8463ef85b22c005fc1943" :answer/id #uuid "e6271ea2-d733-5c9f-a29f-c8d91b5ab3dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2(2+{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72227/selection/0e01a54d31956189b9fb15a26ff26c9a0bd91df0b08651d9c6858d7afc442975" :answer/id #uuid "79ccbd2b-aeb6-5da3-89a2-840bd87940aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(8-3{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72227/selection/02f10a388ca33956376228a75d7487636a828bdb63ebc5365c2c387bbbe5479e" :answer/id #uuid "0d6bfeeb-66e6-568c-9dd3-00acbe026181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(2-8{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72227/selection/e3bd911ae62b8934d520d6ef7a045962412c759bbed3a68ace4883f26b2b3c96" :answer/id #uuid "046e9722-05a5-5b19-b50f-f029cb92380d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8-{e}^{2}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72227/selection/37ef648350f71d8d7922a8c5ec4eff077b886ed05c33a90f3e8ad6bd2f8e31c2" :answer/id #uuid "614d5477-6d94-5213-8e45-0b4d7808110d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(8+2{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72227/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "44772783-fc80-5623-8ee8-fc21629f8da8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72227/selection/0e01a54d31956189b9fb15a26ff26c9a0bd91df0b08651d9c6858d7afc442975" :answer-field/choices ["q-72227/selection/3d84380a08212e1f89ee8af17779262184458ad276b8463ef85b22c005fc1943" "q-72227/selection/0e01a54d31956189b9fb15a26ff26c9a0bd91df0b08651d9c6858d7afc442975" "q-72227/selection/02f10a388ca33956376228a75d7487636a828bdb63ebc5365c2c387bbbe5479e" "q-72227/selection/e3bd911ae62b8934d520d6ef7a045962412c759bbed3a68ace4883f26b2b3c96" "q-72227/selection/37ef648350f71d8d7922a8c5ec4eff077b886ed05c33a90f3e8ad6bd2f8e31c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72227" :question/id #uuid "47f60e14-5051-5f60-9121-3f253fa28394" :question/math-academy-id "q-72227" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x}$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=2\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (4x-3{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2(4\\cdot (2)-3{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s} \\\\  & =2(8-3{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72227/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b47a8b7-722d-564e-8e7a-ad07577d6f6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72227"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342736/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "6c8d67a6-cef9-5d47-98bb-461df3bba6e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342736/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "deeb1edc-4564-5578-bed7-e9fbbfd77deb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342736/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-342736/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342736" :question/id #uuid "a6f176b5-889a-5c1a-aa75-6203cb1a3c50" :question/math-academy-id "q-342736" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1}$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=3\\,\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nThe $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{x+1}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x+1}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3+1}} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of $-1\\text{ }\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342736/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b47a8b7-722d-564e-8e7a-ad07577d6f6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342736"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10899"] :question/problem "Given that $y=x^3+e^x$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}=2$ at the point where $x=1,$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{3}+{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{3}+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}+{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}=2$ and $x=1,$ and solve for $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3\\cdot {1}^{2}+{e}^{1}) \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3+e) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{2}{3+e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10901"] :question/problem "Given that $r=\\sin\\theta$ for $\\theta = \\theta(t),$ and that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d t}=\\sqrt{2}$ at the point where $\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4},$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d \\theta}{\\textrm d t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d t}=\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4},$ and solve for $\\dfrac{\\textrm d \\theta}{\\textrm d t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10902"] :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=x+e^x$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $2 \\,\\textrm{cm}/\\textrm{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=5\\,\\textrm{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (1+{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}=2 \\,\\textrm{cm}/\\textrm{s}$ and $x=5$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2(1+{e}^{5})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
